stimuli.content:
In a certain code:
'P 1 Q' means 'P is the father of Q';
'P 2 Q' means 'P is the daughter of Q';
'P 3 Q' means 'P is the wife of Q';
'P 4 Q' means 'P is the brother of Q';
'P 5 Q' means 'P is the mother of Q'.

Use only the relations that each expression states.

questions.question_text:
In a certain code:
'P ◆ Q' means 'P is a parent of Q';
'P ● Q' means 'P is the sister of Q';
'P ■ Q' means 'P is the husband of Q';
'P ▲ Q' means 'P is the son of Q'.

If 'R ▲ S ■ T ● U ◆ V', how is V related to R?
